=== 3. slip, separated from the cos(delta) geometry ===================
  drive wheel tread turned          109.999 m
  base_link path (ground truth)     106.492 m
  rear axle path (ground truth)     105.453 m
  rear axle path predicted from
    tread * cos(steer), no slip     105.407 m

  NAIVE "slip" = (tread - base_link path) / path   +3.29 %
  REAL  slip   = (predicted - true) rear axle path -0.04 %
  [note] the difference between those two numbers is geometry, not slip: a steered drive wheel travels a longer path than the axle it pushes, by 1/cos(delta), and base_link is offset from that axle again

